super-clipboard (1.6.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Updates: Super Clipboard looks for new releases on GitHub at startup and
    every 12 hours. A notification and a bar in the panel offer "Update",
    which downloads the package, checks its SHA-256 checksum and installs it
    after asking for an administrator password; the new version then starts
    by itself. "Check for updates automatically" in the settings turns the
    check off; super-clipboard --check-update checks from a terminal.
  * Every fix and feature pushed to GitHub is published as a release with the
    .deb attached.
  * The history is saved when the process is stopped, for example by an
    upgrade.

 -- Sacid Sezgin <noreply@localhost>  Wed, 18 Nov 2026 19:44:27 +0100

