super-clipboard (1.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Renamed the product from SuperV to Super Clipboard: package, command
    (super-clipboard, super-clipboard-toggle), application ID
    (org.super_clipboard.Clipboard), icons and the data/config folders
    (~/.local/share/super-clipboard, ~/.config/super-clipboard).
  * English is the default interface language; German is used when the system
    language is German. Language detection now follows gettext rules
    (LC_ALL, LC_MESSAGES, LANG, LANGUAGE preference list; C/POSIX = English).
  * Documentation (README) is now in English.

 -- Sacid Sezgin <noreply@localhost>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0100

superv (1.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Preview: Space shows the full text or the image large; text can be edited
    before it is pasted (Ctrl+Enter). Sensitive entries stay masked until
    "Show" is pressed.
  * Formatted copies (text/html) are stored; a button next to the pin pastes
    them with formatting. The "Paste with formatting by default" setting swaps
    what Enter and the button do. Shift+Enter does the other one.
  * Release notes in the AppStream data, so software centres show what changed.

 -- Sacid Sezgin <noreply@localhost>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0100

superv (1.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Show the panel only once it is in its final place (no flash at the wrong
    position); on Wayland an invisible probe finds the current monitor first.
  * Ctrl+1..9 waits until Ctrl is released before pasting, and also works for
    entries that are scrolled out of view or not in the current tab.
  * New tab "URLs" for web addresses.
  * Names like Mobile_pos2 are no longer treated as passwords.

 -- Sacid Sezgin <noreply@localhost>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +0100

superv (1.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Quick pick: Ctrl+1 to Ctrl+9 pastes the first to ninth entry; the numbers
    are shown on the entries.
  * Each entry shows when it was copied.
  * The panel reopens where it was dragged to, remembered per monitor.
  * Entries older than a configurable number of days are deleted (pinned
    entries stay).
  * Tabs: All, Text, Code, Sensitive, Images. Sensitive entries (passwords,
    tokens, keys, IBANs, card numbers) are shown partly masked.
  * Settings window (gear button in the panel header).

 -- Sacid Sezgin <noreply@localhost>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100

